# Neither harness Dockerfile COPYs anything from the build context, but
# docker still tars the whole context directory to the daemon before
# building. runs/ accumulates per-run workdirs (full repo checkouts,
# node_modules) — gigabytes that would be uploaded on every image build for
# nothing. Excluding them makes both the Pro seal build and the SDLC env
# build start instantly regardless of run history.
runs/
sdk-probe/
# Same reasoning: the shared pnpm store grows to hundreds of MB of package
# tarballs. It is mounted into the container at run time, never COPYed, so it
# has no business in the build context.
.pkg-store/
